##* {{RQ:Swift Advancement of Religion|page=29|passage=And among other Regulations it vvould be very convenient to prevent the Exceſs of Drink, vvith that '''ſcurvy''' Cuſtom among the Lads, and Parent of the former Vice, the taking of Tobacco, vvhere it is not abſolutely neceſſary in Point of Health.}}
##* {{RQ:Swift Journal to Stella|letter=|date=9 January 1711|page=|passage=We only had a '''scurvy''' dinner at an alehouse.}}
