##* {{RQ:Scott Peveril of the Peak|volume=IV|chapter=VIII|page=192|passage=I have a '''scurvy''' touch of old puritanical humour about me. I abide not the imposition of hands—take off your grasp from my cloak, or I will find means to make you unloose it.}}
